//! The Settings shell + the `tui-settings` (external media) sub-page — M5
//! (`docs/goal/ui/settings.md` § Navigation model; `tui.md` § External media
//! handoff; ui.yaml `tui-settings`).
//!
//! **Shell scaffold.** Settings is a top-level tab whose Root is a rail of
//! sub-pages; a sub-page is reached by the two-element `nav` patch
//! (`{"view":"settings","id":"<page>"}` — `settings.md` § Navigation model) or,
//! for a human, by activating its rail row, and `settings-nav-back` returns to
//! the rail. The full account/quota Root (the `settings` ui.yaml page) and the
//! other rail sub-pages (logs, mail-settings, …) are future slices; today the
//! rail lists only the built sub-page.
//!
//! **`tui-settings`.** The one page exclusive to this client (`platforms: [tui]`)
//! — the external-media handoff preference. This terminal can't play audio/video
//! inline (`tui.md` § Declared platform absences 1), so it can hand a clip to the
//! OS default player; whether it does is the user's choice: ask (default) /
//! always / never.
//!
//! **Persistence is client-local.** Unlike the cross-app user prefs that live
//! in the synced account plane (moderation, sync), this is a
//! tui-client-*type*-specific *rendering* preference — no other app has an
//! inline-AV absence, so no other app has the setting. It therefore rests
//! client-local in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fauna-tui/prefs.json`, beside the credential
//! store, written by the UI and never hand-edited (`tui.md` § External media
//! handoff records the resolution). The choice carries no wire / at-rest
//! commitment, so it can move onto the account plane later if it should ever sync.

